# 6. DEFINE SAFE DRAG-AND-DROP BEHAVIOR

We want direct dragging, but arbitrary movement must not break responsive layouts.

Define separate interaction contracts for:

### Section dragging

Move whole sections in the page hierarchy.

### Grid item dragging

Reorder products or categories within a collection.

### Nested container dragging

Move components between compatible containers.

### Element resizing

Change dimensions through corner and edge handles.

### Shape editing

Modify corner radius, supported masks, clipping, and visual geometry.

### Freeform positioning

Allow explicit X/Y positioning in dedicated freeform containers.

### Layout-aware positioning

Use grid placement, flex ordering, gaps, and alignment in normal sections.

### Animation manipulation

Allow supported repositioning of decorative objects without modifying protected animation internals.

For each interaction, specify:

- What the user can drag.
- Which visual handles appear.
- What configuration property changes.
- Which elements can receive a drop.
- How responsive constraints are preserved.
- How conflicts are handled.
- How undo/redo should restore the previous state.
- Whether the operation affects only appearance or also collection ordering.

**IMPORTANT:** Do not make every component absolutely positioned.

Standard storefront sections should retain responsive grid and flex behavior. Absolute positioning should be explicitly enabled only when appropriate.

